--- !u!114 &1231388854
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1231388851}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: ce99abd7e1ae48a42be8118b7db931af, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DialogueEditor
  dialoguePav:
    name: Mom
    sentences:
    - "You\u2019re awfully quiet."
    - "Talk to me bud, I know it\u2019s not what you wanted to hear-"
    - I know.
    - "Woah there Goose, first, this ain\u2019t a punishment. In fact, this\u2019ll
      be a wake up call for all of us to eat healthier."
    - "And second, your body works and diabetes isn\u2019t stupid. It sucks, but
      you\u2019re a tough kid-"
    - "Life doesn\u2019t work like that."
    - "\u2026No. It\u2019s not. But that\u2019s why you gotta love it and love yourself."
    - "Love and loving yourself is hard. It\u2019s easy to do the things we like:
      eating junk, laying around, doing what we want."
    - Oh no. I love you, and what we are gonna do is love each other and get through
      this thing one step at a time.
    - Of course you can.
    - "I don\u2019t see why not, it\u2019s your turkey sandwich."
    - What if? What if is a little thing called conjecture.
    - "Conjecture. Ten dollar word meaning to jump to conclusions. It means you\u2019re
      worried about that next hand life hands you. Work and focus on what you\u2019re
      given right now Timmy, and know that I\u2019m right there if you need me."
    - "Your welcome! And I love you too. Let\u2019s see what all delicious options
      we have here\u2026"
    profile: {fileID: 1387844822, guid: ecef41b7135d00e4b88785fb0ae884a0, type: 3}
  dialogueKid:
    name: Timmy
    sentences:
    - "\u2026"
    - "You know I can\u2019t have donuts anymore?"
    - "Well that\u2019s not fair! Why is it that my pancreas stops producing insulin,
      and all the sudden I\u2019m punished. It\u2019s not my fault my body doesn\u2019t
      work."
    - "Well I like what we eat. You and dad shouldn\u2019t have to change for my
      stupid diabetes."
    - "Yeah but I gotta be a tough kid the rest of my life? There\u2019s gotta be
      a cure or a pill I can take."
    - "Well life\u2019s not fair\u2026"
    - Well what do you mean?
    - Well what if I love candy?
    - Yeah it is, but does that mean I have to love diabetes?
    - Can I see the menu?
    - "\u2026Oh I didn\u2019t know turkey sandwich was on here! Can we cut the crust
      off?"
    - Conjunction?
    - Ok. Thank you for loving me ma, I love you.
    - Yumm...
    profile: {fileID: -1518043225, guid: ea87f947358ed0b4cbe878f498516ca7, type: 3}
  dialogueParent:
    name: 
    sentences: []
    profile: {fileID: 0}
